{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Observations.CrossingEnergyBarSplit","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Observations.CrossingEnergyBarSplit","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.CrossingEnergyBarSplit.undivided_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.CrossingEnergyBarSplit.undivided_eq","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Observations/CrossingEnergyBarSplit.lean#L96-L102","doc":"The q-integer's numerator and denominator, related by the identity that\nmakes the constructive candidate explicit: `qⁿ − q⁻ⁿ = [n]_q · (q − q⁻¹)`.\nStated for an arbitrary `num`, so it is the *algebra* of not-dividing rather\nthan a claim about any particular `n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.CrossingEnergyBarSplit.bar_odd_ratio_is_bar_even","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.CrossingEnergyBarSplit.bar_odd_ratio_is_bar_even","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Observations/CrossingEnergyBarSplit.lean#L85-L94","doc":"**A ratio of two bar-ODD quantities is bar-EVEN.**  This is the mechanism:\n`[n]_q`'s numerator and denominator are each bar-odd, so the bar acts on the\nratio as `(−f)/(−g) = f/g` and the bar-odd content cancels.  Stated\nabstractly — `fb`/`gb` are the barred values, and the hypotheses say each is\nthe negation of its unbarred partner — so it applies to any such ratio, not\nonly to `[n]_q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.CrossingEnergyBarSplit.mirror_swaps","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.CrossingEnergyBarSplit.mirror_swaps","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Observations/CrossingEnergyBarSplit.lean#L77-L83","doc":"**The mirror swaps `n₊` and `n₋`** (`prop:antiparticle-crossing-reversal`\nitem 2: negate, then `q ↔ q⁻¹`).  So the writhe is negated and the crossing\nnumber is preserved: the bar-ODD part is the mirror-invariant one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.CrossingEnergyBarSplit.bar_odd_eq_crossing_number","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.CrossingEnergyBarSplit.bar_odd_eq_crossing_number","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Observations/CrossingEnergyBarSplit.lean#L70-L75","doc":"**The bar-ODD part carries the CROSSING NUMBER.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.CrossingEnergyBarSplit.bar_even_eq_writhe","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.CrossingEnergyBarSplit.bar_even_eq_writhe","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Observations/CrossingEnergyBarSplit.lean#L63-L68","doc":"**The bar-EVEN part carries the WRITHE.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.CrossingEnergyBarSplit.crossingEnergyBar_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.CrossingEnergyBarSplit.crossingEnergyBar_eq","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Observations/CrossingEnergyBarSplit.lean#L56-L61","doc":"`crossingEnergyBar` really is `crossingEnergy` at `q⁻¹` — stated so the\nname is not taken on trust. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.CrossingEnergyBarSplit.crossingEnergyBar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.CrossingEnergyBarSplit.crossingEnergyBar","kind":"def","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Observations/CrossingEnergyBarSplit.lean#L53-L54","doc":"The bar involution `q ↦ q⁻¹` applied to the crossing energy. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.CrossingEnergyBarSplit.crossingEnergy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.CrossingEnergyBarSplit.crossingEnergy","kind":"def","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Observations/CrossingEnergyBarSplit.lean#L47-L51","doc":"The crossing energy of a braid with `np` positive and `nm` negative\ncrossings: `def:crossing-energy` weights `L₊` by `q` and `L₋` by `−q⁻¹`, and\nSUMS them.  The sum, rather than a product, is what makes this inhomogeneous\nin `q` and hence not bar-even. ","signatureChunk":0}]}